% composition-elements: steady beat in 4/4; paired eighth notes and quarter notes; high, middle and low; loud/soft contrast; repeated pop hook; eight-bar AABB movement form
% composition-listen: Carly Rae Jepsen — "Don't Leave Me on the Dance Floor" (2026), included in the CBC Music Top 20 dated 9 November 2026
% composition-listen-url: https://www.carlyraemusic.com/music/
% composition-bridge: Notice the reliable dance pulse, a short memorable vocal hook and the way production drops or adds layers to frame a choice to move.
% composition-context: Carly Rae Jepsen is a British Columbia-born Canadian pop songwriter and performer; CBC's current Top 20 placed this 2026 release among its new Canadian selections.
% composition-distance: Original C-major three-note tune, lyric and C-F-G harmony; no melody, words, bass line, drum pattern or production sound from Jepsen's track is used.
% improv: {"id":"A","bars":"3-4","role":"movement leader","prompt":"How does the hello move?","choices":["two side steps","two shoulder taps","two seated reaches"],"replyBars":2}
% improv: {"id":"B","bars":"7-8","role":"whole class","prompt":"Choose the ending energy","choices":["tiny and soft","bright and strong","freeze in silence"],"replyBars":2}
% dossier-function: original SK dance-pop listening bridge and accessible movement game; the class sings two repeated greetings, follows one selected movement, then chooses the size and energy of the ending
% dossier-elements: eight bars in 4/4, C-major pitch set C-D-E-G, C4-G4 range; quarter notes, paired eighths, half notes and half-bar rests; repeated two-bar hook in bars 1-4, contrasting response in bars 5-8; AABB form; steady beat and soft/strong contrast
% dossier-practice: Rehearsal key C; written range C4-G4. Begin at quarter note = 88 and rise toward 104 only if words and movements stay relaxed. Teach the pulse seated first. Every movement choice has standing and seated versions; a learner may conduct or play the beat instead of moving.
% dossier-accompaniment: Newly authored C-F-G pop loop with optional bass roots on beat 1, clap on beats 2 and 4 and shaker eighths. Keep bars 4 and 8 sparse so the live decision is audible; do not recreate the reference's beat or synth sounds.
% dossier-lyrics: Original English greeting and movement words. Teachers may substitute names or accessible action verbs while preserving the rhythm and crediting the classroom adaptation.
% dossier-honesty: AI-assisted original course composition, 11 November 2026. It is a listening bridge, not a Carly Rae Jepsen song, soundalike, transcription or arrangement.
% dossier-licence: CC0 1.0 for melody, lyric, harmony and ABC. The referenced song and recording remain copyrighted and are linked, not reproduced.
% dossier-respect: Name Jepsen and the source track; use the comparison to hear craft in contemporary Canadian pop rather than treating pop as musically simple or disposable.
% dossier-review: SK classroom teacher, movement/accessibility reviewer, second score reader and student listening trial; all reviews still required
